1. Height for pressure drops below p0 = 100000 Pa (air at 15 C)
   p0 -      1 Pa ->    0.084 m
   p0 -     10 Pa ->    0.844 m
   p0 -    100 Pa ->    8.439 m
   p0 -   1000 Pa ->   84.771 m
2. Near p0, 1 Pa is 0.0843 m; pressure noise of 2 Pa (1 sigma) is about 0.17 m of height noise
3. Same 1000 Pa drop, different assumed air temperature
   -10.0 C ->   77.42 m
    15.0 C ->   84.77 m
    35.0 C ->   90.65 m
4. The weather lowers the ground pressure by 100 Pa during a session;
   the vehicle sits on the ground with the p0 stored at arming: reads +8.44 m
